04", "authorid": 1314, "bench": [1314], "title": "K.Dominic vs The Assistant Executive Engineer on 4 July, 2025", "numcites": 27, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "<b>section</b> 135(1). The offence of theft of <b>electricity</b> is <b>compoundable</b>\n                                  under  <b>section</b> <b>152</b>  of <b>Electricity</b> Act, 2003 and this petitioner, by\n                                  paying ... under  <b>Section</b> 151A  of the <b>Electricity</b> Act, an offence is\n\n                     registered, the question of <b>compounding</b> may not arise. Sub-<b>section</b> (2) of\n\n                      <b>Section</b> <b>152</b>  states", "docsize": 48510, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Madras High Court", "author": "G R Swaminathan", "authorEncoded": "g-r-swaminathan"}, {"tid": 125032329, "catids": null, "doctype": 1024, "publishdate": "2025-11-11", "authorid": null, "bench": null, "title": "Gagandeep Singh vs State Of Haryana And Another on 11 November, 2025", "numcites": 11, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "second offence and, therefore, the matter is not <b>compoundable</b>\n\nunder  <b>Section</b> <b>152</b>  of the <b>Electricity</b> Act, 2003.\n \n 8.           At the very threshold, it becomes imperative ... governed by fundamentally different\n\nprinciples.\n \n 9.            As envisaged under  <b>Section</b> <b>152</b>  of the <b>Electricity</b> Act,\n\n<b>compounding</b> is a creature of statute. Its availability, scope", "docsize": 20139, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Punjab-Haryana High Court"}, {"tid": 78337045, "catids": null, "doctype": 1024, "publishdate": "2023-02-27", "authorid": null, "bench": null, "title": "Surajbhan vs State Of Haryana on 27 February, 2023", "numcites": 9, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "cases)\n\n<b>compounding</b> offences.\n \n 11.          The relevant portion of  <b>Section</b> <b>152</b>  reads as under:\n\n               &quot;<b>152</b>. <b>Compounding</b> of offences. - (1) Notwithstanding anything\n\n      contained in the  Code ... make this <b>Section</b> <b>compoundable</b> is clear\n\n      and writ large from the wordings of  <b>Section</b> <b>152</b>  of the <b>Electricity</b> Act,\n\n      2003. The learned counsel appearing", "docsize": 24053, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Punjab-Haryana High Court"}, {"tid": 56657968, "catids": [1], "doctype": 1007, "publishdate": "2022-03-29", "authorid": null, "bench": null, "title": "M.V.Laksshmi Narasimhan vs The Assistant Executive Engineer on 29 March, 2022", "numcites": 7, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "treated as unauthorized\n\n                use of <b>electricity</b> as per  <b>Section</b> 126  of the <b>Electricity</b>\n\n                Act and not under  <b>Section</b> 135  of the Act. Though the\n\n                petitioner ... offence under\n\n                 <b>Section</b> <b>152</b>  of the <b>Electricity</b> Act. The application was\n\n                considered and the offence was <b>compounded</b> as per  <b>Section</b>\n\n                <b>152</b>  of the <b>Electricity</b>", "docsize": 9037, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Madras High Court"}, {"tid": 170123015, "catids": [228, 7, 4], "doctype": 1002, "publishdate": "2014-05-09", "authorid": 725, "bench": [725], "title": "Om Prakash vs Bses Rajdhani Power Limited on 9 May, 2014", "numcites": 10, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "<b>Section</b> <b>152</b>  of the <b>Electricity</b> Act, there\n\nis no provision either in the  Code of Criminal Procedure  or in the  <b>Electricity</b>\n\nAct  for <b>compounding</b> ... learned counsel for the\n\nrespondent.\n \n 4.       <b>Section</b> <b>152</b>  of the <b>Electricity</b> Act provides as under:-\n\n                  &quot;<b>152</b>.      <b>Compounding</b>       of    offences:   (1)\n                Notwithstanding anything contained", "docsize": 16684, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Delhi High Court", "author": "V K Jain", "authorEncoded": "v-k-jain"}, {"tid": 885707, "catids": [10, 2], "doctype": 1013, "publishdate": "2010-07-01", "authorid": 1189, "bench": [1189], "title": "R.Vijayan vs State Of Kerala on 1 July, 2010", "numcites": 9, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "<b>Sec</b>. 379 read with  <b>Sec</b>. 34  of I.P.C. Since theft of <b>electricity</b>\n\nwas <b>compoundable</b>, the petitioner has <b>compounded</b> the offence\n\nunder  <b>Section</b> <b>152</b> ... towarding the <b>compounding</b> fee. Sub  <b>Section</b> 2  and\n\n 3  of  <b>Sec</b>. <b>152</b>  of the <b>Electricity</b> Act reads as follows:-\n\n               &quot;(2)  On payment", "docsize": 4585, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Kerala High Court", "author": "V Ramkumar", "authorEncoded": "v-ramkumar"}, {"tid": 152230541, "catids": null, "doctype": 1021, "publishdate": "2025-03-04", "authorid": 1294, "bench": [1294], "title": "Yagya Sharan Patel vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 4 March, 2025", "numcites": 4, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "<b>compoundable</b> offence\n                           by imposing an additional penalty amount of Rs.3000/- for <b>compounding</b> the\n                           offence in terms of  <b>Section</b> <b>152</b>  of the <b>Electricity</b> ... which has been levied against the\n                           petitioner was <b>compounded</b> in terms of  <b>Section</b> <b>152</b>  of the <b>Electricity</b> Act,\n                           2003 by the department themselves. A decision", "docsize": 29864, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Madhya Pradesh High Court", "author": "V Mishra", "authorEncoded": "v-mishra"}, {"tid": 92623450, "catids": null, "doctype": 1004, "publishdate": "2024-11-13", "authorid": null, "bench": null, "title": "Vinod Mannalal Jain vs State Of Mah on 13 November, 2024", "numcites": 4, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "only  <b>section</b> 135  of <b>Electricity</b> Act, but\n\neven  <b>section</b> 138  of <b>Electricity</b> Act is permitted to be <b>compounded</b> by\n\ninvoking  <b>section</b> <b>152</b>  of <b>Electricity</b> ... <b>compound</b>\n\n <b>section</b> 138  of <b>Electricity</b> Act in spite of <b>electricity</b> authorities\n\naccepting <b>compounding</b> charges.  In support of his submissions that\n\neven  <b>section</b> 138  of <b>Electricity</b>", "docsize": 16076, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Bombay High Court"}, {"tid": 171230324, "catids": [13], "doctype": 1010, "publishdate": "2021-09-15", "authorid": 614, "bench": [614], "title": "Mahendra Kumar Mittal vs State Of Chhattisgarh on 15 September, 2021", "numcites": 4, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "submits that\n    the offence alleged against applicant is <b>compoundable</b> under\n     <b>Section</b> <b>152</b>  of the <b>Electricity</b> Act. Hence applicant may be\n    enlarged on anticipatory bail ... fact that offence alleged\n    against applicant is <b>compoundable</b> under  <b>Section</b> <b>152</b>  of the\n    <b>Electricity</b> Act, without commenting anything on merits of case,\n    I am inclined", "docsize": 8950, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Chattisgarh High Court", "author": "P P Sahu", "authorEncoded": "p-p-sahu"}, {"tid": 195463119, "catids": [7, 4], "doctype": 1017, "publishdate": "2015-11-03", "authorid": 828, "bench": [828], "title": "Premjibhai Govindbhai Panjri & 2 vs State Of Gujarat & on 3 November, 2015", "numcites": 5, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "question \u00a0 is \u00a0 whether \u00a0 the \u00a0 offence\u00a0\n         should\u00a0be\u00a0<b>compounded</b>\u00a0or\u00a0not.\u00a0 <b>Section</b>\u00a0<b>152</b> \u00a0of\u00a0the\u00a0\n         <b>Electricity</b>\u00a0Act,\u00a02003\u00a0provides\u00a0for\u00a0<b>compounding</b>\u00a0of\u00a0\n         offence:\u00ad\n               &quot;<b>152</b>.\u00a0<b>COMPOUNDING</b> ... amount,\u00a0the\u00a0respondent\u00a0\n         No.2\u00a0be\u00a0directed\u00a0to\u00a0<b>compound</b>\u00a0the\u00a0offence.\u00a0 <b>Section</b>\u00a0\n         <b>152</b> \u00a0of\u00a0the\u00a0<b>Electricity</b>\u00a0Act\u00a0no\u00a0doubt\u00a0provides\u00a0for\u00a0\n         <b>compounding</b> \u00a0 of \u00a0 an \u00a0 offence", "docsize": 10688, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Gujarat High Court", "author": "J B Pardiwala", "authorEncoded": "j-b-pardiwala"}], "found": "21 - 30 of 1188", "encodedformInput": "electricity%20%22section%20152%22%20compounding%20doctypes%3Ahighcourts"}